<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Carrowmore</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Carrowmore megalithic cemetery</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Carrowmore is a large cemetery of megalithic tombs on the Cúil Irra peninsula near Sligo in north-west Ireland. Its dozens of passage tombs and stone circles, some dated to the 4th millennium BCE, are among the oldest in Ireland. It lies below Knocknarea, whose summit cairn is linked by legend with Queen Medb.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/carrowmore.jpg" alt="Carrowmore" width="320" height="181" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Andreas F. Borchert · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Carrowmore_Megalithic_Cemetery_P7_2015_09_08.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
